White light is used to illuminate the double slit in Young&#39;s double-slit experiment. Which of the following is/are true?&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><strong>I.</strong></td><td>The central fringe will be white.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>II.</strong></td><td>Closest bright fringe to the central fringe will be a violet fringe.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>III.</strong></td><td>There will not be any dark fringe.</td></tr></tbody></table>
1. <strong>I</strong> only<br>2. <strong>I</strong>, <strong>II</strong><br>3. <strong>I</strong>, <strong>III</strong><br>4. <strong>I</strong>, <strong>II</strong>, <strong>III</strong>
